   804	  `(2.1)` establishes tube disjointness, and rigidity is justified by dominance of
   805	  the `k_*` term as `R -> infinity`, not by a pole identity off its vertex class.
   806	* **Prime label/derivative.** `p'`, `q'` are genuine derivatives. `Pi`, `Pi_i`,
   807	  `X = Pi_1 = Pi_3`, `Y = Pi_2` are distinct symbols, never conflated; the two
   808	  campaign symbols `b` are separated explicitly in §7 R3.
